# Spring Boot Datastore Sample

This project is based on the Google Cloud Codelab "Spring Data and Cloud Datastore".

## Overview

- Spring Boot application using Google Cloud Datastore as the persistence layer.
- Follows the codelab example for configuring Datastore, defining entities, and exposing REST endpoints.

## Setup

1. Enable Cloud Datastore in your Google Cloud project.
2. Set `GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS` to the path of your service account JSON key.
3. Build and run the Spring Boot application.

## Notes

- This repository contains the sample code structure and configuration for the codelab.
- Use the codelab link for step-by-step instructions and additional context.

Codelab: https://codelabs.developers.google.com/codelabs/cloud-spring-datastore?hl=es-419#7